proposals.proposal:
The active tab gets:
- a 56×32 pill in accentSubtle behind its icon (radius pill);
- its label in Rubik 700;
- its icon at full accent.

When a tab screen mounts, the pill pops in with scale .8→1 and an opacity fade over 140ms using spring.pop. Each screen owns its own nav, so a sliding pill would need a shared navigator layout, and the pop-in is enough. Inactive tabs show the pressedOverlay pill while pressed.

proposals.problem:
The fixed chrome around the board is about 400 dp, from layout.game in the tokens:
- 2P cards: 160 dp;
- bar and lock strip: about 64 dp;
- gaps: 16 + 20 + 16 dp;
- keypad: 60 dp; cancel: 44 dp;
- paddings: 8 + 12 dp (GameScreen.tsx:1391, 1690-1700).
Insets come on top. The board gets min(width − 32, what is left) (screens/game/geometry.ts:53-57), and the keypad is given the same width (GameScreen.tsx:1513-1518). Estimates:
- 360×740 with a 48 dp nav bar: a board of about 268 dp (cells ~28 dp), keys ~26 dp wide;
- 360×640: a board of about 170 dp, keys ~16 dp wide;
- a larger Android display-size setting has the same effect.
Nothing tests short heights (model.test.ts:143-146 checks widths only).

proposals.proposal:
Give each key a 3 dp lip, a darker keyBg drawn as a View offset under the face (the tokens' Android-safe recipe):
- the face sits on the lip, and the press lands flush on it;
- armed: the lip is P1 at about 35%, so the row glows ready when I hold a lock;
- idle: the lip is grey;
- complete: no lip (flat), with BRD-7's check;
