- Pirates: chunky wooden slab;
- Castle: blackletter-serif;
- Robots: 7-segment LCD (segments can flicker as gimmicks);
- Monsters: gooey and dripping;
- Football: varsity block jersey numbers;
- Circus: marquee bulbs;
- Wild West: wood-type Clarendon;
- Space: rounded futuristic;
- Chefs: soft dough;
- Heroes: bold italic comic.

evals.effort:
Rough sizes in Claude working days, each a focused session with tests and the visual check loop:

- Phase 0, presentation fixes: 2-3 days. Worth doing even if the set never changes.
- Phase 1, vertical slice (2 characters × 2 looks, plus a board mock): 1-2 days, plus Moshe's review.
- Phase 2, series infra (protocol, retired map and chain, server migration, personas, bot-only list, 3×3 picker, i18n scaffolding, about 81 fixture files): 4-6 days.
- Phase 3, Rig 2:
  - digit templates and attachment points: 2-4 days;
  - nested limbs, per-avatar motions, crossfade, idle life, style update: 6-10 days.
- Per series:
  - drawn by Claude at the invested bar: 3-5 days (9 characters, check loops);
  - from illustrator masters: 2-3 days;
  - translations: about 0.5 day.
- Refresh the existing 10 digits onto Rig 2 ('Originals'): 2-3 days.
- Optional Skia renderer: 7-12 days, higher risk.
- Optional Rive: 4-6 days of integration, plus an external animator per series.
- Optional unlocks: series unlockLevel with server enforcement and an 'unlocked' moment, 2-3 days [NEW FEATURE: enabling content the spec plans for V1.1].

Recommended launch package: Phase 0, 1, 2 and 3 core, the Originals and 3 new series. About 25-40 days, roughly 5-8 weeks. Phase 0 alone can ship before the store release, while the series are built.

What Moshe must decide:
- replace all of the set, or keep the Originals and the bots;
- the number of series at launch versus the release date;
- whether he will pay an illustrator or animator;
- style rules (outline and gradient allowed?);
- the in-cell face crop;
- 0 in or out;
- unlocks now or later;
- the cast changes.

